;Y combinator, or the fixed point evaluator is a primitive built-in
factorial → (λ self x. 
 if == x 0
 then 1
 else (* x (self (- x 1)))p
)
(Y(factorial) 10)

; Y combinator does the following step:
; Y(f(function, x)) = Y(f(f,x))
; Since the function itself is passed to itself, it can re-run itself
; This is essentially the same as referencing the function inside itself.
